Monsoon Bias Bureau is a five-member acoustic-electronic ensemble built around the principle that the bowed instrument owns pitch motion while the acid synthesizer owns timbral motion.

**Ananya Rao** — sarangi, meend architecture, sympathetic-string resonance, arrival phrasing.

**Leon Mercer** — acid sequencer, mono synth, filter automation, negative-space drum design.

**Meera Kulkarni** — prepared electric piano, arrival chords, modal checkpoints.

**Sameer Naik** — khanjira, woodblock, acoustic percussion substitution, phrase punctuation.

**Jon Bell** — bass clarinet, low acoustic shadow, sub-free transitions, key-noise texture.

There is no conventional frontperson. Ananya defines continuous pitch movement; Leon keeps the electronic note grid deliberately stubborn; Meera confirms destinations after the fact; Sameer makes the pulse tactile without adding density; Jon supplies low acoustic air when the sequencer withdraws. Live versions vary because bow pressure, room humidity, sympathetic-string response, filter calibration, and the exact length of each glide alter the relationship between BEND and ARRIVE.

